On Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:15:53 -0700, Pat Maddox wrote:
> When sending the notification, include the inbox count, e.g. "(inbox N)"
> at the end, so I know when processing is done.

Done in "[PATCH] src/lab-process-mail: Report the inbox count in each
notice" [1]. After each pass the loop runs notmuch count tag:inbox and
ends the notice with the result, e.g. "answered: <subject> (inbox 3)".
An answered notice with "(inbox 0)" means processing is finished. The
stuck notice gets the count too, so you can see how much is waiting
behind the stuck message.

The count comes from notmuch after the pass, not from the agent. The
tests check both notices.

The patch applies to b/dev@upstream. It only touches the notify lines
and the header comment, so it applies with or without "[PATCH]
src/lab-process-mail: Quiet jj and name each message" [2].

